        <div class="reveal-left" data-v-45fa8901="">
          <div class="text-fg-subtle mb-3 flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-[0.65rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase" data-v-45fa8901=""><span class="bg-accent inline-block h-px w-6" data-v-45fa8901=""></span> the color story </div>
          <h2 class="mb-5 font-mono leading-[0.95] font-bold" style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);letter-spacing:var(--tracking-tightest);" data-v-45fa8901=""> Eight hues,<br data-v-45fa8901="">one feeling </h2>
          <p class="text-fg-muted mb-4 text-[0.92rem] leading-[1.75]" data-v-45fa8901=""> Nothing is saturated enough to cause fatigue. The dark variant rests on a muted blue-gray base; the light variant shifts the same roles toward ink-on-paper. </p>
          <p class="text-fg-muted mb-6 text-[0.92rem] leading-[1.75]" data-v-45fa8901=""> Accents follow a strict hierarchy — <span class="font-mono text-[0.85rem]" style="color:#83afe5;" data-v-45fa8901="">blue</span> → <span class="font-mono text-[0.85rem]" style="color:#9a93e1;" data-v-45fa8901="">purple</span> → <span class="font-mono text-[0.85rem]" style="color:#80c1ca;" data-v-45fa8901="">teal</span> — and the semantic roles never drift: green is success, salmon is error, yellow is a type or a warning. </p>
          <div class="border-line flex items-center gap-4 border-t pt-6" data-v-45fa8901="">
            <div class="border-line h-[88px] w-[88px] shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-[6px] border shadow-[0_8px_24px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12)]" data-v-45fa8901=""><img src="/images/grimicorn-mascot.png" alt="Grimicorn — a skeletal rainbow unicorn" class="h-full w-full object-cover" loading="lazy" data-v-45fa8901=""></div>
            <div class="text-fg-muted font-mono text-[0.68rem] leading-[1.7]" data-v-45fa8901="">
              <div class="text-fg mb-0.5 text-[0.72rem] font-semibold" data-v-45fa8901=""> Grimicorn </div> grim reaper <span class="text-accent" data-v-45fa8901="">×</span> unicorn —<br data-v-45fa8901="">dead serious, secretly colorful.
            </div>
          </div>
